<title>FRANCE: Key union recommends Elf workers continue strike.</title>
<headline>Key union recommends Elf workers continue strike.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's largest union said on Thursday it would recommend that striking Elf refinery workers keep up their action after company concessions on pay failed to address strikers' concerns over job cuts.</p>
<p>&quot;The proposals are scandalous,&quot; Marc Deluzet, head of the CFDT's oil industry branch, said after talks between Elf management and unions on a week-old strike at Elf French plants.</p>
<p>&quot;They are trying to buy an end to the conflict with money but they have not addressed the essential thing, jobs,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>&quot;Our position is to pursue the strike, but it is up to staff to decide,&quot; he said. Other unions may have other views, he said.</p>
</text>
